| Type of Server Maintenance | Description |
|----------------------------|-------------|
| Hardware maintenance | Check fans, power supplies, RAID status, and temperatures; clean dust from vents and heatsinks; replace failed disks or PSUs per procedure. Hot-swap components where supported; power down when required. Record all actions in the maintenance record. |
| OS maintenance | Patches, updates, and role or feature updates; backup before major changes; schedule reboots and communicate downtime. Apply updates in a test environment first where possible. Rollback procedure should be documented. |
| Server maintenance record | Log date, asset, type of maintenance (preventive or corrective), tasks performed, parts replaced, downtime, and sign-off. Used for audit, warranty, and planning. |


