| Key Term | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| RAID status | RAID arrays show status (e.g. OK, degraded, failed). A degraded array has one failed disk; replace the disk and rebuild before a second failure. A failed array may require data recovery; backup and monitoring reduce risk. |
| Hot-swap | Components (e.g. disk, PSU) can be replaced without powering off the server. Follow the manufacturer procedure (e.g. prepare for removal, wait for LED, remove, insert new, wait for rebuild). |
| Maintenance window | A scheduled time when the server can be rebooted or taken offline. Communicate to users and stakeholders; complete tasks within the window and document any overrun. |


